{
  "id": 90099775,
  "iid": 2235,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "CMake: Remove most checkAPI uses restricting \"termoutput\"",
  "description": "Remove checks forbidding the use of fprintf() and g_warning(),\ni.e. \"terminal output functions\", everywhere except in\nepan/dissectors/* and dissector plugins.\n\nThis was introduced in 58b8fef9ea5160a7cca6fc57a0cd563a186f1dd8\nwith the comment:\n\t# Wireshark should not write to stdout (?)\n\t# (Of course tshark should!)\n\nIt's not clear what purpose this ban serves but it seems intended\nto remind developers that Wireshark is a graphical program? Or maybe\npeople were developing dissector plugins and testing with tshark only?\n\nWhatever the case let's limit this unusual restriction to dissector\ncode only. Good diagnostic output, to the terminal or elsewwhere, is\notherwise considered important and encouraged. These functions are\nimportant and useful tools for development and debugging purposes.\n\nThis will be followed by another commit removing the various ugly\nhacks people have been using to get around this restriction.",
