    },
    {
      "id": "2d1a4b08525ee50b7bc56d9e6495385c82da2d64",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 518791453,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I don't know the situation exactly for Windows, but we can use `g_debug()`, and install a different log handler on that platform if necessary. MR for g_debug incoming.\n\nBut I don't see the problem with Linux, and even if it is a problem, I don't see how this checkAPI thing is a proper solution. It's extremely heavy handed and frustrating to deal with.",
